[{"id":77982,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Super.20Lie.20n-algebra.20extensions.2C.20higher.20WZW.20models.20and.20super.E2.80.A6/near/77982\">#152</a> We are working on a followup: </p>\n<p><em><strong><a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/Super-exceptional%20embedding%20construction%20of%20the%20M5-brane\">Super-exceptional embedding construction of the M5-brane</a></strong></em></p>","timestamp":1563371871,"subject":"Super Lie n-algebra extensions, higher WZW models and super…","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":78117,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Super.20Lie.20n-algebra.20extensions.2C.20higher.20WZW.20models.20and.20super.E2.80.A6/near/78117\">#153</a> … and now with considerably strengthened main theorem (summary <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/files/SuperExceptionalEmbeddingConstruction.jpg\">here</a>)</p>","timestamp":1564007115,"subject":"Super Lie n-algebra extensions, higher WZW models and super…","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":78128,"sender_id":25,"sender_full_name":"David_Corfield","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7d52fbe20c8ac05886a296e9ee2159b1?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Super.20Lie.20n-algebra.20extensions.2C.20higher.20WZW.20models.20and.20super.E2.80.A6/near/78128\">#154</a> Looks intriguing. Here are some typos</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>superymmetric; non-pertrubative; hmotopy; super-valume; cocyle; intersting; an hence; MO9-projectin</p>\n</blockquote>","timestamp":1564038186,"subject":"Super Lie n-algebra extensions, higher WZW models and super…","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":78130,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Super.20Lie.20n-algebra.20extensions.2C.20higher.20WZW.20models.20and.20super.E2.80.A6/near/78130\">#155</a> Thanks! Fixed now.</p>","timestamp":1564041376,"subject":"Super Lie n-algebra extensions, higher WZW models and super…","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":78250,"sender_id":25,"sender_full_name":"David_Corfield","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7d52fbe20c8ac05886a296e9ee2159b1?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Super.20Lie.20n-algebra.20extensions.2C.20higher.20WZW.20models.20and.20super.E2.80.A6/near/78250\">#156</a> Utterly trivial, but I keep tripping on your ‘quest’ sentences when I start reading the article</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>In the quest to mathematically formulating M-theory,…</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>is grammatically awkward. Perhaps, “In the quest for the mathematical formulation of M-theory”</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>In the quest for shedding some light in that direction,…</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>the ‘quest’ here is too weak. They have aims like the Holy Grail. Perhaps, “Looking to shed some light in that direction,…”</p>","timestamp":1564471087,"subject":"Super Lie n-algebra extensions, higher WZW models and super…","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":78273,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Super.20Lie.20n-algebra.20extensions.2C.20higher.20WZW.20models.20and.20super.E2.80.A6/near/78273\">#157</a> Thanks!</p>\n<p>This, and a bunch of other little things, now improved (hopefully) in the latest version (<a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/Super-exceptional%20embedding%20construction%20of%20the%20M5-brane\">here</a>).</p>","timestamp":1564584718,"subject":"Super Lie n-algebra extensions, higher WZW models and super…","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]},{"id":78274,"sender_id":25,"sender_full_name":"David_Corfield","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7d52fbe20c8ac05886a296e9ee2159b1?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Super.20Lie.20n-algebra.20extensions.2C.20higher.20WZW.20models.20and.20super.E2.80.A6/near/78274\">#158</a></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>prinicples; has be systematically obtained; gauged-of-gauge; cohomoloy; correspong; geoemtry</p>\n</blockquote>","timestamp":1564592933,"subject":"Super Lie n-algebra extensions, higher WZW models and super…","stream_id":15,"display_recipient":"Mathematics, Physics & Philosophy","reactions":[]}]